utils/clipsai_resize/ is a copy of the `resize` package from Clips AI 0.2.1
(https://github.com/ClipsAI/clipsai), used under the MIT License. The full license
text, including the Clips AI copyright notice, is in LICENSE in this directory.

The copy is not verbatim. Each module's docstring lists its local changes; in summary:

- clipsai.media.video_file.VideoFile  -> video_file.VideoFile, a value object holding
  the five properties the package reads, probed once with ffprobe by the caller.
- clipsai.utils.pytorch / .conversions -> compute.py, which reimplements the three
  functions used without psutil or pynvml.
- clipsai.media.editor.MediaEditor    -> dropped; it was assigned and never used.
- clipsai/resize/resize.py            -> not copied. It was the Pyannote-diarizing
  entry point; utils/reframe.py drives the Resizer instead, with speaker segments
  taken from the cached Scribe transcript.
- Segment gained a `found_face` flag and detect_scenes gained a time window.

Nothing in this directory imports WhisperX or Pyannote.
